# shipped-hook-sums — the checksum of every version of the Keel hooks that has been on main or in a release (dir #683).
#
# install-secret-guard.sh treats a hook as Keel's only when its line 2 is the marker line AND its whole body is one of
# the versions listed here. A hook that carries the marker but matches none of them was edited after install (or comes
# from a build this list does not know), so it is the user's data: a plain re-install refuses, and --force backs it up
# to <hook>.pre-keel.bak before replacing it. Without this list a re-install overwrote such an edit silently.
#
# One line per version: <hook name> <cksum CRC> <cksum byte count> — exactly what `cksum < <hook>` prints after the name.
# POSIX cksum, so it needs neither git nor a repo and prints the same on macOS, GNU and busybox. This guards against
# an accidental or deliberate EDIT of a hook; it is not a security boundary.
#
# WHEN YOU CHANGE tools/secret-guard/pre-commit OR pre-push: ADD one line for the new body here and KEEP the old ones
# (an older install must still be refreshed, not refused). tests/test_secret_guard_writes.sh fails until you do — it
# checks that the shipped hooks are listed and, wherever the clone has tags, that every body a release tag carried is.
# To print the line for the current body:   printf "%s " pre-push; cksum < tools/secret-guard/pre-push

